    {
      "rank": 3,
      "row_id": 284641,
      "chunk_id": "7e7360d2d6e5_1",
      "doc_id": "7e7360d2d6e5",
      "text": "I find myself moving the phone top different positions in my hand, or switching hands because it's sort-of cramping. Because it's considerably larger than my S6, it's also heavier, and I stand by the belief that the lack of a good case makes it more uncomfortable and heavy. I'm waiting for a couple of cases to help change my thoughts. Speed First, I have to say that I thoroughly am grateful for the speed of the phone. It launches very quickly through the apps, through the web, and basically anything I'm trying to accomplish. Battery The battery has been very generous. I was able to watch a one and a 11⁄2 hour video, and I think it only took like a 5% to do so, which I didn't pay attention until the end that it only took that much. I was very impressed and surprised. It charges very quickly.",
      "score": 0.036671432581885606,
      "brand": "Samsung",
      "model": "Galaxy S9 Plus",
      "rating": 4,
      "timestamp": "2020-02-19",
