    {
      "rank": 5,
      "row_id": 203341,
      "chunk_id": "916d464a58b3_1",
      "doc_id": "916d464a58b3",
      "text": "Why not make it wider? I want a big screen, not a small one. If I want a small screen, I'll get that kind of phone. It is fast, and it does accept a lot of apps, but that's the only benefit. And Bixby! The button on the side that you hit accidentally far too often announces Bixby, Samsung's faulty attempt to outdo Siri and Google. It is worse than annoying; with the phone on silent and media sound to zero, it still loudly proclaims, Hi! I'm Bixby! I have never used it and never will. It alone is reason enough to run away from this phone. The battery life isn't that good either. I have to charge it daily, which I was hoping I wouldn't have to do. I want a phone that lasts for several days without charging, and this isn't it.",
